# @flibbertigibbeting/loading-message - Cursor Rules

When working with loading states in this project:

## Preferred Patterns

### Quick async operations (<2 seconds expected)
Use `<Spinner />` for simple visual feedback:
```tsx
import { Spinner } from '@flibbertigibbeting/loading-message'

{isLoading ? <Spinner type="dots-bounce" size={24} /> : <Content />}
```

### Longer operations (2-10 seconds)
Use `<LoadingMessage />` to keep users engaged:
```tsx
import { LoadingMessage } from '@flibbertigibbeting/loading-message'

{isLoading && (
  <LoadingMessage
    messages={["Loading...", "Almost there...", "Just a moment..."]}
    interval={2000}
    spinnerType="circle"
  />
)}
```

### Custom loading logic
Use the `useLoadingMessage` hook:
```tsx
import { useLoadingMessage } from '@flibbertigibbeting/loading-message'

const { message, isComplete, reset } = useLoadingMessage({
  messages: ["Step 1...", "Step 2...", "Done!"],
  interval: 1500,
  loop: false
})
```

## Spinner Types by Use Case

- **Minimal/Professional**: `circle`, `dots-fade`, `bars`
- **Playful/Engaging**: `dots-bounce`, `orbit`, `pacman`
- **Progress-like**: `progress-bar`, `meter`, `ring-resize`

## Accessibility

Components include accessibility by default:
- `aria-live="polite"` for screen reader announcements
- Respects `prefers-reduced-motion` automatically
- No additional a11y work needed

Override the label for context:
```tsx
<Spinner type="circle" label="Loading your dashboard" />
```

## Common Patterns

### Button with loading state
```tsx
<button disabled={isLoading}>
  {isLoading ? <Spinner type="dots-bounce" size={16} /> : 'Submit'}
</button>
```

### Full-page loader
```tsx
<div className="fixed inset-0 flex items-center justify-center bg-white/80">
  <LoadingMessage 
    messages={["Loading your experience..."]}
    spinnerType="orbit"
    spinnerSize={48}
  />
</div>
```

### Inline loading
```tsx
<span className="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
  <Spinner type="circle" size={14} />
  Saving...
</span>
```
